<span id="A2.F10.3.1.1.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A2.F10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{0}|\bm{x}_{100})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">100</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{0}|\bm{x}_{100})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.F10.3.1.1.12.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">:</span></span>
<span id="A2.F10.3.1.1.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.F10.3.1.1.12.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:258.8pt;">
<span id="A2.F10.3.1.1.12.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F10.3.1.1.12.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">not wish to abide by a personal talks meeting point . On any cake , and you can search a pallet for a " Grease . " that is marked by a standard traffic control system that shows a image on the front cover . We still believe that people vote for their candidate . Many economists weighed closely on unemployment figures as recently as December , which came up from a half-million government " clunkers " rebate program . But , funny it may seem , rational person decided to advance press freedom rather than encourage senior activists as try</span></span>
</span></span></span>
</span>
</span><span id="A2.F10.3.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="A2.F10.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Using an absorbing-state D3PM model (trained on LM1B with 128 denoising steps) to complete test-set examples at different noise levels. We corrupt the example using <math id="A2.F10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, then iteratively sample from <math id="A2.F10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t-1}|\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t-1}|\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> to reconstruct. Mask token shown as “<span id="A2.F10.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3B3;">[M]</span>”.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
